.nh
.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-auth-login - Sign in with the browser (creates a time-limited API key for this profile)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro auth login [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the Gyro panel in your browser; you approve the request there (permissions and expiry are chosen on that page)
and the new key is stored in the profile, exactly like 'gyro configure'. No key is copied by hand.
Over SSH or without a display the address is only printed: open it on any device where you are signed in.
In CI keep using a key: echo "$KEY" | gyro configure --token-stdin


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for login

.PP
\fB--keyring\fP[=false]
	store the key in the OS keychain

.PP
\fB--no-browser\fP[=false]
	only print the address, do not open a browser

.PP
\fB--scopes\fP=""
	preselect scopes (comma separated, e.g. cloud_read,services_read); you can still change them in the browser

.PP
\fB--template\fP=""
	preselect a permission template: readonly, dns, cloud, containers, storage, billing, full


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--account\fP=""
	act in another account you are a panel user of (id from \fBgyro account list\fR; "self" = your own; env GYRO_ACCOUNT, profile default: \fBgyro account use\fR)

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gyro auth login
  gyro auth login --profile work --no-browser
  gyro auth login --template readonly
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgyro-auth(1)\fP
